From 30a496396fcf3bd0b41c8b9af784a67a4e6b0af3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ville=20Kivel=C3=A4?= <vkivela@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 06:15:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/31] push: answer a subscription alike in a window that
 keeps nothing

PushManager.subscribe() asked the application for the notifications
permission in an off-the-record profile before it said no. The engine
has no push service unless the application switches one on, and where
there is none Chromium hides that in an off-the-record profile: it asks
for the notifications permission, assumes the embedder will deny it, and
rejects with INCOGNITO_PERMISSION_DENIED whatever the answer. An
embedder that asks its reader gets a question that leads nowhere, and a
site tells the two profiles apart, because an on-the-record profile
rejects at once with SERVICE_NOT_AVAILABLE and no question.

PushMessagingManager::Register() now answers SERVICE_NOT_AVAILABLE
whenever there is no push service, in every profile, and the request
for the permission, its callback and the console message that went with
it are gone. Notification.requestPermission() does not go through this
code and is unchanged.

pushSubscribeAnswersAlikeOffTheRecord subscribes from a page on each
kind of profile and checks that the application is never asked and the
page hears the same error; off the record it was asked once without this
patch. notificationRequestStillReachesTheApplicationOffTheRecord checks
that a request to notify still reaches the application there.

See villekivela/omaweb#421.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
